:: Task Intro Field Test [event] {"position":"3500,4500","size":"100,100"}
/* Task introduction for Field Test (task_sister_field_test), the day after The Gym Meeting (main_gymMeeting).
   $gymOwner.name agreed to the pilot $darius.name asked for: two test units in the girders of his flagship, and access to
   the chain's own camera system so the readings can be matched to what people are doing. The cameras now show up on my
   dashboard. What's missing is real data from someone who really trains, with a sensor on. I send $sister.callName:
   she's fit, and the footage will look good in a pitch. She works out that I can watch.
   Establishes: the gym, the sensor, and the camera she knows about. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[13].img>><</silent>>
$gymOwner.name's answer came in at twenty to six this morning, presumably between sets. $darius.name has it printed out on his desk, which he does with anything he intends to argue with, and he's already gone over it with a yellow highlighter.

He waves me over before I've got my jacket off.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "He's agreed to the pilot. Two units in the ceiling of his flagship from Thursday, and two of his other locations without them, for comparison. I'm almost moved." },
{ who: $player, text: "That was fast. I figured he'd want the dinner first." },
{ who: $darius, text: "He still wants the dinner. This is the part he doesn't consider a commitment. He's also given us access to the building's camera system, so we can match the readings to what people are actually doing at the time." },
{ who: $player, text: "He just handed over his cameras?" },
{ who: $darius, text: "He asked whether they'd be useful, and I said they would. I believe he took it as a compliment to his gym." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I look over at my own screen on the way back to my desk. $ethan.name has been busy: there's a new tile on the dashboard, labeled in his usual style <i>GYM (do not show $gymOwner.name)</i>, and behind it a grid of grainy little feeds. Treadmills, a squat rack, the smoothie bar, the front desk with its wall of glowing logo. A man in a tank top is doing curls in front of a mirror and talking to his own reflection.

<<linkreplace "Ask what the problem is">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "The difficulty is the sensor data. His members won't be wearing our sensors, and I'd rather not build a retention study on people who don't know they're in one. That tends to end with a lawyer." },
{ who: $player, text: "So what do you need?" },
{ who: $darius, text: "One person who trains properly, three or four times a week, and keeps a sensor on from the moment they walk in until they leave. Somebody who actually works out, rather than someone who's there to be measured." },
{ who: $player, text: "You look like you work out." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I do. But I'd be measuring myself, and then interpreting my own numbers, and I'd trust the result about as much as I trust his body fat figures." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Across the office, $sister.callName is standing at the printer in a blouse with her sleeves pushed up, tapping her foot while it warms up. She runs four mornings a week, has since high school, and she complains about her gym near campus every time she comes home from it: the broken lockers, the guy who grunts, the one working shower.

And somebody is going to have to make a video for the pitch, eventually. Footage of a gorgeous gym full of people having a great time is a lot easier to sell when one of those people is gorgeous too.

<<linkreplace "Call her over">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Hey, are you busy for the next few weeks?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "That's an ominous way to start a conversation. Why?" },
{ who: $player, text: "How would you feel about working out at $gymChain.name a few times a week, on company time, with a free membership and a little sensor taped to your wrist so $darius.name gets his numbers?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Wait, the one in the old warehouse? With the smoothie bar?" },
{ who: $darius, text: "The smoothies are eleven dollars. I'd consider that part of the study." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Let me get this straight. You want me to skip the office, go to the nicest gym in the city, and you're calling it work." },
{ who: $player, text: "It is work. There's data involved, and he'll want to talk to you about it afterwards, at length." },
{ who: $sister, text: "That does sound like work." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She leans over my shoulder to look at what I've got open, and I don't bother closing it. She sees the grid of feeds, and I can tell exactly when she recognizes the smoothie bar.

<<linkreplace "Let her look">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Is that live? That's the gym, right now?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Their cameras. It's for the study, so we can line the readings up with whatever people are doing." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So you'll be sitting here, at your desk, watching me sweat." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'll be watching a heart rate graph. You'll be a very small part of a very large spreadsheet." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Sure. A spreadsheet." },
{ text: "She taps the little square with the squat rack in it, just once, with one fingernail, like she's marking a spot on a map." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Then I'd better have good form." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She goes back to the printer, which has finally decided to print, and I hear her laugh at something on her phone on the way. $darius.name is already writing her name at the top of a new spreadsheet column. I leave the gym tile open in the corner of my screen.

<<EndTaskIntro "task_sister_field_test" "Back to work">>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
